  "description": {
    "raw": "You gain the ability to see through solid rock as if it were transparent glass. You may see through 1 foot of stone per caster level. You see within the stone as if you were looking at the area in normal light, even if there is no illumination, though low-light vision and darkvision have no effect on your ability to see through stone. Metal at least 1 inch thick or wood or dirt at least 3 feet thick blocks your vision.\n\nThe spell does not negate concealment for those creatures hiding behind stone objects (the stone is still an obstacle to your attacks).",
    "search_text": "\"you gain the ability to see through solid rock as if it were transparent glass. you may see through 1 foot of stone per caster level. you see within the stone as if you were looking at the area in normal light, even if there is no illumination, though low-light vision and darkvision have no effect on your ability to see through stone. metal at least 1 inch thick or wood or dirt at least 3 feet thick blocks your vision.\\n\\nthe spell does not negate concealment for those creatures hiding behind stone objects (the stone is still an obstacle to your attacks).\"",
